<p>So this didn't work for me personally due to the reasons stated by 5239 itself. I'd be fine with it if it just wanted to pull off the cool necromancer-shtick on their own and try to fulfill a fantasy that only young adults would want when given DnD-esque magical powers, but their reason being that it's another &quot;My parents don't understand/respect my chosen gender identity&quot; comes off derivative, if not clichéd when it comes to writing genderqueer characters.</p>
